Z||000000||lowfierogt||12-16-2001||01:33 PM||||Has anyone used a ribbed molding facia on a 86 GT?    Can you cut off the ribbed molding and put on the smooth one?<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/lowfierogtsig.gif">         <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT Project, fastback V8<BR>87 coupe Getting V6 daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-16-2001||01:39 PM||||I'm about to do the same thing.  It looks like it's pretty easy to modify the molding to the round style.  either cutting it down and adding round or using repair compound to modify the ribbed style.<BR>I am considering losing the side marker and making the whole spot molding and adding a small side marker light to the fascia or fender.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||12-16-2001||01:44 PM||||Yes it will work.  I am putting an 87 SE front nose on my 87 GT.  I had to cut the moulding off, but the new rounded moulding will cover what you cut off.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
